Image 1 is a sprite sheet of the WHOLE video: frames every 2 seconds, left-to-right, top-to-bottom, cell i = i*2 seconds. Images 2-4 are full-resolution frames (first frame, then two text-heavy moments). Use the sprite sheet for TIMING and COVERAGE (what text appears when, what stays, what changes) and the full-resolution frames for EXACT SPELLING (accents, punctuation, casing, emojis). Do not limit yourself to the full-resolution frames: text that appears only in the sprite sheet must be included too. Ignore the app end card (app icon, app name, App Store / Google Play badges, download CTA) entirely.

Return {"wall_text": [{"text": string, "start": number, "end": number, "persistent": boolean, "position": "top|center|bottom|other", "style": string}], "captions": [{"text": string, "start": number, "end": number}], "all_wall_text": string}. wall_text = designed overlay text (hook, headline, title, labels, bullets). A text visible in most frames is ONE entry with persistent=true spanning its full range. If a wall text changes (new line, new headline), close the old entry and open a new one. captions = burned-in subtitles that follow speech; merge consecutive caption fragments into readable phrases, use the voiceover script below to fix spelling. all_wall_text = every distinct wall_text in order, joined with newlines.

